Really? Like which drives? teledisk allowed you to do it on a PC, but that 
required certain drives, in combination with a full reprogramming of the floppy 
controller, which also required certain floppy controllers, since not all of 
them could handle it. And it was not something for the faint of heart, and I 
believe it still wasn't perfect.

And I still fail to see the point of switching to another format, since the PRO 
floppies probably makes very little sense using on anything but on a PRO, which 
still will have RX50 drives.
And no, putting some other floppy drive in the PRO will probably not work either.

