Well, teledisk is available on the net. However, from what I've read it also 
requires a rather slow PC to work (timing issues). A program like PUTR is 
probably better. But for the rest, the same hardware is required anyway.

Replacing the RX50 with a RX33 in the PRO... Hmm, might work, but I would never 
bet money on that. The PRO expects the floppy to look a specific way, and 
probably don't appreciate deviations. The RX33 must somehow tell if it's playing 
RX50 or PC-format. That's something the real RX50 can't tell. Is that done via 
some pin on the interface, or is it some software thing?

