>> And no, putting some other floppy drive in the PRO will probably not work either.
> 
> Why? (Seriously, see above.)

First of all, no matter what drive, it would have to be RX50 format on it. The 
device driver in the PRO knows about the physical layout on the floppy, and acts 
based on that. If you have another number of sectors/track, another number of 
sectors, or anything not RX50-like, the software will not deal with it 
graciously, and will definitely not work right.

If you have a RX33, it can play with RX50 media, but will it look the same from 
an interface point of view? I suspect there are some additions, or deviations.

