> as well as a testing and production system.  And an ethernet card!! :-)

:-)
I don't know how much RSX you know, but P/OS is really cute. They set up a 
special region for the graphics memory map, and have a special driver that plays 
with it, and then they implement an abstract graphics layer, and do a lot of 
really neat tricks in RSX to make it work really smooth. They've used the 
capabilities of RSX really neat. Also some daemons that are running from time to 
time to deal with some background tasks. In same ways much neater than DOS ever 
was, and neater that Windows today.

Oh, and I think you have a bitmap of the character cells somewhere as well, 
since it's all software rendering, from what I've gathered. It would be fun to 
look at RT-11 drivers for the PRO sometime. (But that's really a project for a 
sunny day... :-) )

