Actually, the RX01 is an industry standard IBM format. All diskettes for 8" were 
preformatted, so that wasn't a DEC idea. The special RX02 format is DEC 
specific, but you can reformat a floppy between RX01 and RX02 mode.

But for 5.25" floppies, DEC really was obnoxious.

