And they didn't.

>> In RSX, the RX33 and RX50 devices are handled by the general MSCP driver. P/OS 
>> have a special driver to deal with the hardware in P/OS, so there is no 
>> similarity or shared code for this.
> 
> Bad thing.  :-(

Yes. From our point of view, here and now.
However, MSCP is a complicated beast. I suspect that the controllers in the PRO 
are more streamlined and adapted to the specific task at hand.
(But a proper MSCP controller would have been nice, I think.)

