>>>>>
>>>>> And, now something else new.  You mentioned the Pro software only
>>>>> running on the Pro.  What are the incompatabilities between the Pro
>>>>> and other PDP-11 systems? And, has anyone ever looked what it might
>>>>> take to add a"Pro" option to SIMH?
>>>> A lot! The PRO have a different bus, which is memory mapped. Each slot is 
>>>> allocated a memory area, and peripehrials are accessed through that, and not 
>>>> through an I/O page like "normal" PDP11s. Second you don't have a console on a 
>>>> PRO in the same sense as on other PDP11s. No device for that in the I/O page. 
>>>> Instead you have the keyboard mapped somewhere (raw I think), and then you have 
>>>> the bitmap graphics memory, on which you write to make stuff appear on the screen.
>>>>
>>>> So all dealings with hardware outside the CPU is unique to the PRO.
>>> That's interesting. I was under the impression that the PRO could run
>>> normal PDP-11 software (mine is running RT-11 and I assumed it was not
>>> a custom version but just plain old RT-11.  It was on it when I got it!)
