>> RT-11 have a few special device drivers to deal with the PRO as well. As long as 
>> you use the device drivers to communicate, you'll be fine. However, if you try 
>> to play with the hardware directly, you won't get far with programs from a 
>> "normal" PDP-11. The most obvious problem will be that you don't have the 
>> console DL-11, which *any* normal PDP-11 will have.
> 
> I need to fire mine up (I have never actually done anything with it, it
