> it has normal RT-11 device drivers,like I thought, or a set of PRO specific
> ones.  I have the software sourcebook 2 volume set and I certainly don't
> remember seeing a special version of RT-11 for the PRO being listed in there.

RT-11 have special drivers for the PRO as well. It must have, otherwise it 
wouldn't work.
I also happen to know as much. Can't remember the name of the device drivers, 
though.

>>> As for the built in Keyboard/display, My Terak's all do that too.  But it
>>> is mapped to the address of a normal PDP-11 console so real PDP software
>>> runs just fine.  Plus, you can turn it off and set the serial port to
